{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.b\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.b</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Law_of_Cosines)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Vector_Bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Vector Bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Complex_Numbers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Complex Numbers)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5.b_(Complex_Numbers_-_Simpler)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5.b (Complex Numbers - Simpler)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Cheese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Cheese)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Under_4_minutes)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Under 4 minutes)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math4All999_(pretty_easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math4All999 (pretty easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the degree measure of the acute angle formed by lines with slopes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/380b7d522ad99a045644f976f00a00936d0d233f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~30\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~37.5\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~45\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~52.5\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"425\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Remind that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4732830a5b1b1ed2eda5d0fb5b0cfa5fe9aaebaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{slope}=\\dfrac{\\Delta y}{\\Delta x}=\\tan \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"39\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle between the slope and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33bdc6adefb64e3275bd08a1dfc7df7605e03740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1=2=\\tan \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c70aabc8f485d1b951c36be88f900b151b54fb68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_2=\\dfrac{1}{3}=\\tan \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />. The angle formed by the two lines is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fc0f8a46a8e4714980858a0a86065a3a3ae5a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha-\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1a1ecebc994239eda1c218fc260c458c84ca05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\alpha-\\beta)=\\dfrac{\\tan\\alpha-\\tan\\beta}{1+\\tan\\alpha\\tan\\beta}=\\dfrac{2-1/3}{1+2\\cdot 1/3}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"374\" height=\"45\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82ca712caa7a5ebaaf315419a324dc7f76f522d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha-\\beta=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"137\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~plasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can take any two lines of this form, since the angle between them will always be the same. Let's take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/c/20c311147b479df529d837e7da1ff0428df1f75a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> for the line with slope of 2 and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47aa3cf580d59a96ce4161a8b001458aa3317cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\frac{1}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"37\" /> for the line with slope of 1/3. Let's take 3 lattice points and create a triangle. Let's use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb913ad463dcc2916d4135977f0d06f20ad93cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04c2d1bd65c882efed8513bbbf77022aba66364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. The distance between the origin and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb913ad463dcc2916d4135977f0d06f20ad93cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. The distance between the origin and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04c2d1bd65c882efed8513bbbf77022aba66364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4f56670a613c679c0291375283e37df33f3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. The distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bb913ad463dcc2916d4135977f0d06f20ad93cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04c2d1bd65c882efed8513bbbf77022aba66364.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />. We notice that we have a triangle with 3 side lengths: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e93b4bff537e8b63a0a3db030fbb756ab27255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/4/1c4f56670a613c679c0291375283e37df33f3a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. This forms a 45-45-90 triangle, meaning that the angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f1edbb211b1a97049e363dd06427443a2b8748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"39\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.b\">Solution 2.b</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.b\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG, allow the line with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to pass through point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/f/84fe60729c37515dec723a57cf2ac0c6c5ce369e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O = (0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5fdcfb4e88678ce8b88a2baed0a0e776a95575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = (1, 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />, and the line with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> to pass through point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e98dad6876ad584ad78ba7ba85df79c7ab86aad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (3, 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"81\" height=\"20\" />. Notice that the slope of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c29b01eebceac41bac571e6cf543b747d18d5582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1 - 2}{3 - 1} = -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"98\" height=\"40\" /> and is hence perpendicular to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/c/37ca7a38f7eed488e5f646482c71b0cf56222e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Drawing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc13f0783d8b0092bce37b79f5696127bec4586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d729b8f9ecc5ea48d7a1fa1c767c9501568d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{OA} = \\overline{AB} = \\sqrt{(1)^2 + (2)^2} = \\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"256\" height=\"35\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc13f0783d8b0092bce37b79f5696127bec4586.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle OAB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles right triangle. Therefore, the desired angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/9/c09e5f544ade36bdc0042bf64776932a7c64fbe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 45^\\circ}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"158\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ka-maths\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Law_of_Cosines.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Law_of_Cosines)\">Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Law of Cosines)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Follow Solution 2 up until the lattice points section. Let's use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f4d1e83d6eef61f31d78844deb189c54a7abc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc7c549288e4950e0691e299461a101213daff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. The distance between the origin and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f4d1e83d6eef61f31d78844deb189c54a7abc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/8/e6895445d6df3d71da8e88786be997603e1b9032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. The distance between the origin and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc7c549288e4950e0691e299461a101213daff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c5549b2882221591ac2ce7921f8b69decba231c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. The distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f4d1e83d6eef61f31d78844deb189c54a7abc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc7c549288e4950e0691e299461a101213daff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(9,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6d1b584a42c88275d2ae86a59079aad25c034f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. Using the Law of Cosines, we see the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29cc263160e27fad6d334ea63a40a84cddfc589a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 = 90 + 20 - 2\\times\\sqrt{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44d3d6b0902aa533bb19e296a02f15131d8861e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\times\\sqrt{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"21\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f60a2a2478abeebc101750a22dcc6bbc40a0552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\times\\cos(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the angle we are looking for. \n</p><p>Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8eeb56af20838218c4be2d371f15d9dbf7f9e182.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-60 = -2\\times(\\sqrt{20}) \\times(\\sqrt{90}) \\times\\cos(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"291\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d01f07321d30286ea932ad5a563194c4a4d3bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 =  \\sqrt{1800} \\times\\cos(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"166\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870b04e044de9927bda8cc13a0dc6cd990379825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 =  30\\sqrt{2} \\times\\cos(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/caccaaa2a61b238e85cc328b44591be6c71a9322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}= \\cos(\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85afdf87f1633d8c26823ea047ab8e5046cb449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~Failure.net\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Vector_Bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Vector_Bash)\">Solution 4 (Vector Bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Vector Bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can set up vectors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866e10e36aa7be83f3ea7dfdc0001712c7ca84f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{a} = &lt;1,2&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/2/1f214019e513ae1baf3661f36a5e523321a9d812.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\vec{b} = &lt;3,1&gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"23\" /> to represent the two lines. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53b45ae68e0d8c49dba61c10d200be981603a88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\vec{a} \\cdot \\vec{b}}{|\\vec{a}| |\\vec{b}|} = \\cos \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"104\" height=\"52\" />. Plugging the vectors in gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afa2024aab6f1436cb447887aa93ef374996107a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta = \\frac{5}{5\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"152\" height=\"43\" />.  From this we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85afdf87f1633d8c26823ea047ab8e5046cb449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} 45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~middletonkids\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Complex_Numbers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Complex_Numbers)\">Solution 5 (Complex Numbers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Complex Numbers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def56ea8536fd1306cf785ef896fc27c5d303fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_1 = 3 + i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc9e035f5fc14ca965949bc1d913bf3e12049a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_2 = 1 + 2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d654942b63a301e6e796edbd19ee64b3181cd09f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Z_2 &amp;= Z_1 \\cdot re^{i\\theta} \\\\ 1+2i&amp;=(3+i) \\cdot re^{i\\theta} \\\\ 1+2i&amp;=(3 + i) \\cdot r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta) \\\\ 1+2i&amp;=3r\\cos\\theta - r\\sin\\theta  + 3ri\\sin\\theta + ri\\cos\\theta \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"355\" height=\"95\" />\n</p><p>From this we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/c/78ce75264246b6e30947c7581d36fea192c581dc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} 1 &amp;= 3r\\cos\\theta - r\\sin\\theta \\\\ 2 &amp;= r\\cos\\theta + 3r\\sin\\theta  \\end{align}\" width=\"347\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>To solve this we must compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce8bad7e9715c5040ba1869126d94cd6463654d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} r &amp;= \\frac{|Z_2|}{|Z_1|} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"68\" height=\"143\" />\n</p><p>Using elimination we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/7/c9706b63ffa4ab3cafe0e023908d9ab7a7abd455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot(2) - (1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bdf76ffe678955c790a8b9262865a49b3b0547.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 5 &amp;= 10r\\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{1}{2r} &amp;= \\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{1}{2\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} &amp;= \\sin\\theta \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} &amp;= \\sin\\theta \\\\ \\theta &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}  45^\\circ} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"123\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5.b_.28Complex_Numbers_-_Simpler.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5.b_(Complex_Numbers_-_Simpler)\">Solution 5.b (Complex Numbers - Simpler)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5.b (Complex Numbers - Simpler)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/def56ea8536fd1306cf785ef896fc27c5d303fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_1 = 3 + i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/c/8bc9e035f5fc14ca965949bc1d913bf3e12049a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_2 = 1 + 2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/2/b421caa518aa7400489d2673bd40ffd3af0e321f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} Z_2  &amp;= Z_1 \\cdot re^{i\\theta} \\\\ 1+2i &amp;=(3+i) \\cdot re^{i\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{1+2i}{3+i} &amp;= re^{i\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{(1+2i)(3-i)}{(3+i)(3-i)} &amp;= re^{i\\theta} \\\\ \\frac{3+2+6i-i}{(3+i)(3-i)} &amp;= re^{i\\theta} \\\\   tan(\\theta) &amp;= 5/5  \\\\  \\theta  &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}  45^\\circ} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"231\" height=\"254\" />\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aac19c0e094885eb71fe32c15b52381b8e5d1e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2x, y = \\frac {1}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"120\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> form a large right triangle and a small right triangle. Call the angle that is formed by the x-axis and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8d3f41e4ce3512f73fcda8ef2c9c236f7143a41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, and call the angle that is formed by the x-axis and the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17efea36f383d3622314b0a912bc2968bf378d6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac {1}{3}x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" />. We try to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e143513513f5ced91b83cbb35f32e317aad63a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\alpha - \\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> first, and then try to see if any of the answer choices match up. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/1/9e143513513f5ced91b83cbb35f32e317aad63a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\alpha - \\beta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/6/2c695a9e1dbaa716f757bd8c00ab8abf8f2cee3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7342501e7962f0d6b1e6285466b3d42ba54e3ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e0fe8149d01441ff4c8dc37aec304effcbed23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0de8ac3aa0141ebb385492cbbe6f978f6c73b655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\alpha$\" width=\"38\" height=\"8\" />. \n</p><p>Using soh-cah-toa, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195b2e72361493bd85a0cc228566f574b1bf1ffb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\alpha = \\frac {2}{\\sqrt 5}, \\sin \\beta = \\frac {1}{\\sqrt 10}, \\cos \\alpha = \\frac {1}{\\sqrt 5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"302\" height=\"43\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05c6465bad4f15e4b5b07b38c6981ac916a9ab5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\beta = \\frac {3}{\\sqrt 10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" />. \n</p><p>Plugging it all in, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2aa731fea1d26d65f08df6a3de52b44edb32c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\alpha - \\beta) = \\frac {5}{\\sqrt {50}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"145\" height=\"43\" />, which is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/6/7361cca6b98c680bdbab5a289fa1e53fa20eac0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sqrt 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"30\" height=\"43\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/13218b20b74236edb1388d9d335134410d8b00b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin (\\alpha - \\beta) = \\frac {\\sqrt 2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"43\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d62cffa3272ccb17e887156557680582ee0f83e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha - \\beta = 45^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/1/981ac3ab9f6e4e18959ddcd00c6e21310fae0186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(C)} 45^{\\circ}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"68\" height=\"30\" />. \n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h1><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Cheese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Cheese)\">Solution 7 (Cheese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Cheese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>AMC 12 does not allow graph paper or protractor. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://amc-reg.maa.org/manual/AMC1012B.pdf\">https://amc-reg.maa.org/manual/AMC1012B.pdf</a>\n</p><p>Using a makeshift ruler, draw an accurate to-scale diagram. You can do this by simply drawing the two lines such that they intersect at the origin. Then, measure the angle by eye or by folding paper to observe that they form a 45 degree angle.\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f1edbb211b1a97049e363dd06427443a2b8748a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{45^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"39\" height=\"26\" />.\n</p><p>~InstallHelp_Hex\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28easy_to_digest.29_by_Power_Solve\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=Uh4K33tNEzBOXc_h&amp;t=1406\">https://youtu.be/YXIH3UbLqK8?si=Uh4K33tNEzBOXc_h&amp;t=1406</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Under_4_minutes.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Under_4_minutes)\">Video Solution (Under 4 minutes)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Under 4 minutes)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/PWBEUXTtUxI\">https://youtu.be/PWBEUXTtUxI</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/kPcsTZpFzTY\">https://youtu.be/kPcsTZpFzTY</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math4All999_.28pretty_easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math4All999_(pretty_easy)\">Video Solution by Math4All999 (pretty easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math4All999 (pretty easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/sa2HHgMZjSg?feature=shared\">https://youtu.be/sa2HHgMZjSg?feature=shared</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A\">2023 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving